From 9cbf7cef4a7bc9ff52b4ad2bbc90e5a8addbbc68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:40:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] rtc: macsmc: clear the PMU's alarm-fired bit when arming

When the alarm goes off the PMU clears the enable bit (0x1401 bit 6) and
sets bit 1 of the same byte. While bit 1 stays set, the next alarm still
clears the enable bit at its second but sets no event and raises no
interrupt. The first version wrote bit 6 alone, through a one-bit NVMEM
cell, so only the first alarm after boot worked: in the smoke test the
awake alarm fired and the three rtcwake s2idle cycles after it slept
until the owner touched the machine (10.1 h, 39 min, 16 min).

Checked on the J414s with the handler unbound: with bit 1 set, the alarm
second clears 0x40 and nothing else happens; after writing 0x01 to the
byte, the same alarm sets the event bit and SPMI interrupt 2 again. With
bit 1 clear, an rtcwake-style s2idle woke on the alarm after 30.1 s
(pm_wakeup_irq = the RTC's interrupt) ahead of a 90 s backup timer.

The cell becomes the whole control byte; arming and disarming clear
bits 6 and 1 and leave the rest (bit 0 reads 1, meaning unknown) as
found.

